1109-01-01" notAfter="1109-12-31">1109</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2551</idno><idno type="APIS">3786</idno><note type="comment">See [BAQ9MH4T]: 193 for the main events of his life.&#13;
&#13;
Three manuscript editions of his writings and translations were deposited respectively in rNgog Blo ldan shes rab's tomb, in the monastery of gSang phu (probably in the main assembly hall), and in Drin las kyi sde (ID:4357) ([7FZ3B926]: 107).</note></person><person xml:id="person4006"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rigs pa'i ral gri</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">རིགས་པའི་རལ་གྲི</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dar ma rgyal mtshan</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos kyi rgyal mtshan</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bcom ldan ral gri</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bcom ldan rigs pa'i ral gri</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rig pa'i ral gri</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bcom ldan rigs ral</persName><birth notBefore="1227-01-01" notAfter="1227-12-31">1227</birth><death notBefore="1305-08-29" notAfter="1305-08-29">1305-08-29</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P1217</idno><idno type="APIS">4006</idno><note type="comment">On his career, see [KHA9ZVGP]: 3-8.&#13;
The dates 1227-1305 are known from the biography (see work (ID:7016)) composed by his student bSam gtan bzang po (ID:4005) ([KHA9ZVGP]: 3).&#13;
His name in religion was Dar ma rgyal mtshan or Chos kyi rgyal mtshan ([FZ6N88AU]: 406) - the name Chos kyi rgyal mtshan is given as his "real name" (mtshan dngos) in a homage by Rong ston ([KM47ZZDJ]: 657 and n. 62). &#13;
The majority of the colophons of his works name him "bCom ldan ral gri," a few "Rigs/Rig pa’i ral gri" or just "Ral gri." Schwabland's discussion of the variants “Rigs pa” and “Rig pa” does not come to a definite conclusion as to which is the correct spelling ([CTQMVBPR]: 2-3).&#13;
He was born as the son of a local wealthy headman, the fourth of five sons and his birth is reported to have been foretold by Śākyaśrībhadra (ID:6418) when he was invited by Ral gri's paternal uncle ([KHA9ZVGP]: 3).</note></person><person xml:id="person4074"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">brtson 'grus dpal</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">བརྩོན་འགྲུས་དཔལ</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">4074</idno></person><person xml:id="person4097"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dpang lo tsA ba blo gros brtan pa</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">དཔང་ལོ་ཙཱ་བ་བློ་གྲོས་བརྟན་པ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dpang blo gros brtan pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">btsun chung lu gu</persName><birth notBefore="1276-01-01" notAfter="1276-12-31">1276</birth><death notBefore="1342-01-01" notAfter="1342-12-31">1342</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2085</idno><idno type="APIS">4097</idno><note type="comment">A short biography from the Shel dkar chos 'byung is translated in [N35FPQ6L]: 62-70. It gives a fire-male-mouse year (1276) as birth-date, and Gyam in Zur rtso as its birthplace. He took novice vows when he was five years old at 'Brog rdo gling, and was ordained at seven.</note></person><person xml:id="person4593"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">Anonymous</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཨཱནོཉམོཨུས</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">4593</idno></person><person xml:id="person5193"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bzang ldan pa dkon mchog grags</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">བཟང་ལྡན་པ་དཀོན་མཆོག་གྲགས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shAkya'i btsun pa dkon mchog grags</persName><birth notBefore="1400-01-01">after 1400</birth><death notAfter="1499-12-31">before 1499</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P5954</idno><idno type="APIS">5193</idno></person><person xml:id="person5999"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bu ston rin chen grub</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">བུ་སྟོན་རིན་ཆེན་གྲུབ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bu ston thams cad mkhyen pa</persName><birth notBefore="1290-01-01" notAfter="1290-12-31">1290</birth><death notBefore="1364-07-01" notAfter="1364-07-01">1364-07-01</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P155</idno><idno type="APIS">5999</idno></person></listPerson><listBibl><bibl xml:id="work3706"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">abhisamayālaṃkāra</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">abhisamayālaṃkāranāmaprajñāpāramitopadeśaśāstrakārikā</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shes rab kyi pha rol tu phyin pa'i man ngag gi bstan bcos mngon par rtogs pa'i rgyan zhes bya ba'i tshig le'ur byas pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mngon rtogs rgyan</title><author ref="person:3756">asaṅga</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><idno type="APIS">3706</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work3711"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">abhisamayālaṃkāravṛtti</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shes rab kyi pha rol tu phyin pa'i man ngag gi bstan bcos mngon par rtogs pa'i rgyan zhes bya ba'i 'grel pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'grel chung</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">abhisamayālaṃkāranāmaprajñāpāramitopadeśaśāstravṛtti</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sphuṭārthā</title><author ref="person:3712">haribhadra</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><idno type="APIS">3711</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work5192"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mngon rtogs rgyan gyi 'grel pa lung gi dpag bsam rgyan 'gyur gyi tshal</title><titl